From b1e48fe897abc2f041edd88c726afb11db8b2d84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 02:18:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stage 282: the return path had no index to return through

The probe asked the tape about a value and looked for the subject in what
came back. It never came back: the main posting list is built with the
slot's own value excluded, so the words of a value can never retrieve the
slot that holds it. probe_hit_rate was 0.000 by construction, and the
teacher treated a miss as a veto, so it fell silent on every family -
clean included - and BC copied that silence into the policy: coverage
0.016 on the train tape, 0.035 held out, on an exam where 280 answered
54%.

Three changes. The probe gets its own index that does not hide values,
and only the probe reads it, so a question still cannot retrieve its own
answer. A probe miss weakens a claim instead of vetoing it: with a lead
of two or more the teacher answers anyway, which also fills the miss
bucket that G_probe_filters_wrong_answers needs in order to compare.
And two gates could not see the collapse - a teacher abstaining on
everything scores the abstain reward on everything, which cleared
G_teacher_usable, and a policy matching it by being equally silent
cleared G_reaches_teacher. Both now ask about answering, not only
about reward.

